1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,074
Ever notice specks or cobwebs drifting across your vision?

2
00:00:03,394 --> 00:00:10,043
Most of the time that's harmless - but if the number suddenly jumps, or part of your view goes dark, that's a different story.

3
00:00:10,363 --> 00:00:16,510
Eye floaters happen when clumps in the vitreous, the clear gel filling your eye, cast shadows on your retina.

4
00:00:16,830 --> 00:00:26,189
Aging is the top cause - the vitreous turns watery and pulls away from the retina over time, something most people go through by 65.

5
00:00:26,509 --> 00:00:30,907
There's no drop or pill that removes them; your brain typically adapts.

6
00:00:31,227 --> 00:00:39,612
High myopia and diabetes raise the stakes, since a thinner retina or fragile blood vessels are more likely to tear or bleed.

7
00:00:39,932 --> 00:00:49,169
One small study also found an antioxidant nutrient blend left about 70% of users with smaller, less bothersome floaters.

8
00:00:49,489 --> 00:00:57,447
The signs to take seriously: a sudden flood of new floaters, flashes of light, or a curtain-like shadow over part of your vision.

9
00:00:57,767 --> 00:01:01,739
Those can signal a retinal tear - see an eye doctor right away.

10
00:01:02,059 --> 00:01:03,733
Floaters on their own are common.

11
00:01:04,053 --> 00:01:06,031
Just remember those warning signs.
